1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:04,302
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,886 --> 00:00:06,429
Earth.

3
00:00:06,763 --> 00:00:08,640
Fire.

4
00:00:08,932 --> 00:00:10,600
Air.

5
00:00:11,309 --> 00:00:14,812
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,355 --> 00:00:19,359
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,734 --> 00:00:23,530
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:23,738 --> 00:00:27,158
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

9
00:00:27,492 --> 00:00:31,120
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

10
00:00:31,246 --> 00:00:32,872
an airbender named Aang.

11
00:00:32,997 --> 00:00:35,208
And although his
airbending skills are great,

12
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:38,002
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

13
00:00:38,086 --> 00:00:39,087
AANG: Oof.

14
00:00:39,212 --> 00:00:42,215
But I believe Aang can save the world.

15
00:00:48,096 --> 00:00:50,139
NARRATOR: ( READING )

16
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:53,059
The Avatar has kidnapped my daughter.

17
00:00:54,185 --> 00:00:58,523
I want you to do whatever it takes
to bring her home.

18
00:01:02,485 --> 00:01:03,903
Augh!

19
00:01:04,279 --> 00:01:05,655
Sandbenders, shoo!

20
00:01:05,738 --> 00:01:07,198
Away from the bison!

21
00:01:07,615 --> 00:01:09,200
Library's sinking...

22
00:01:09,325 --> 00:01:10,785
Library's sinking!

23
00:01:12,704 --> 00:01:14,205
( ROARS )

24
00:01:17,875 --> 00:01:19,002
TOPH: No!

25
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:20,420
I'm sorry, Appa.

26
00:01:20,878 --> 00:01:21,921
Where's Appa?

27
00:01:22,589 --> 00:01:23,715
( GROANS )

28
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:36,561
( WIND BLOWING )

29
00:01:36,644 --> 00:01:38,563
MOMO: ( PURRING )

30
00:01:42,859 --> 00:01:44,444
How could you let them take Appa?

31
00:01:44,611 --> 00:01:45,820
Why didn't you stop them?

32
00:01:46,029 --> 00:01:47,405
I couldn't!

33
00:01:47,488 --> 00:01:50,283
The library was sinking,
you guys were still inside, and...

34
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:51,951
You could've come to get us.

35
00:01:52,035 --> 00:01:53,119
I could've saved him!

36
00:01:53,202 --> 00:01:55,204
I can hardly feel any vibrations out here.

37
00:01:55,288 --> 00:01:58,124
The sandbenders snuck up on me,
and there wasn't time for...

38
00:01:58,207 --> 00:01:59,292
You just didn't care!

39
00:01:59,375 --> 00:02:00,501
You never liked Appa!

40
00:02:00,585 --> 00:02:01,711
You wanted him gone.

41
00:02:01,919 --> 00:02:03,046
Aang, stop it.

42
00:02:03,129 --> 00:02:05,340
You know Toph did all she could.

43
00:02:05,423 --> 00:02:06,591
She saved our lives.

44
00:02:06,883 --> 00:02:08,426
Who's gonna save our lives now?

45
00:02:08,509 --> 00:02:10,094
We'll never make it out of here.

46
00:02:10,303 --> 00:02:12,805
That's all any of you guys
care about, yourselves.

47
00:02:13,222 --> 00:02:15,475
You don't care whether
Appa is okay or not.

48
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:19,354
We're all concerned,
but we can't afford to be fighting, now.

49
00:02:20,605 --> 00:02:22,065
I'm going after Appa.

50
00:02:22,357 --> 00:02:24,359
Aang, wait!

51
00:02:26,944 --> 00:02:28,738
We'd better start walking.

52
00:02:28,821 --> 00:02:31,407
We're the only people who know
about the solar eclipse.

53
00:02:31,491 --> 00:02:33,951
We have to get that information
to Ba Sing Se.

54
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:39,624
You think if we dig out
the giant owl, he'll give us a ride?

55
00:02:43,670 --> 00:02:46,172
( GROANING )

56
00:02:46,798 --> 00:02:48,257
Maybe we should make camp.

57
00:02:48,341 --> 00:02:51,594
No, please, don't stop just for me.

58
00:02:52,553 --> 00:02:55,014
( MOANING )

59
00:02:58,226 --> 00:03:00,103
( GROANS )

60
00:03:01,437 --> 00:03:03,147
( GRUMBLES )

61
00:03:03,648 --> 00:03:05,191
What now?

62
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:17,704
Colonel Mongke, what a pleasant surprise.

63
00:03:18,204 --> 00:03:20,540
If you're surprised we're here,

64
00:03:20,623 --> 00:03:23,626
then the Dragon of the West
has lost a few steps.

65
00:03:29,882 --> 00:03:31,759
You know these guys?

66
00:03:31,926 --> 00:03:36,389
Sure, Colonel Mongke
and the Rough Rhinos are legendary.

67
00:03:36,723 --> 00:03:40,852
Each one is a different kind
of weapon specialist.

68
00:03:40,977 --> 00:03:44,313
They are also
a very capable singing group.

69
00:03:44,731 --> 00:03:47,066
We're not here to give a concert!

70
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,193
We're here to apprehend fugitives.

71
00:03:49,569 --> 00:03:51,529
Would you like some tea first?

72
00:03:51,612 --> 00:03:52,739
I'd love some.

73
00:03:52,822 --> 00:03:54,115
How 'bout you, Kahchi?

74
00:03:54,198 --> 00:03:57,452
I make you as a jasmine man.

75
00:03:57,535 --> 00:03:58,619
Am I right?

76
00:03:59,162 --> 00:04:01,539
MONGKE: Enough stalling, round 'em up!

77
00:04:03,082 --> 00:04:04,500
( GRUNTING )

78
00:04:19,932 --> 00:04:21,434
( GRUNTS )

79
00:04:25,313 --> 00:04:26,439
Ah!

80
00:04:42,789 --> 00:04:44,665
It's nice to see old friends.

81
00:04:44,749 --> 00:04:48,002
Too bad you don't have any old friends
that don't want to attack you.

82
00:04:48,085 --> 00:04:49,253
Hmm...

83
00:04:49,337 --> 00:04:52,089
Old friends that don't want to attack me?

84
00:05:00,723 --> 00:05:03,476
( PANTING )

85
00:05:04,519 --> 00:05:05,520
Unh.

86
00:05:05,603 --> 00:05:07,104
Can't you watch where you're...

87
00:05:07,188 --> 00:05:09,315
- No.
- Right, sorry.

88
00:05:09,732 --> 00:05:11,776
Come on, guys, we've gotta stick together.

89
00:05:12,151 --> 00:05:15,571
If I sweat anymore, I don't think
stickin' together will be a problem.

90
00:05:15,822 --> 00:05:18,032
Katara, can I have some water?

91
00:05:18,407 --> 00:05:21,369
Okay, but we've gotta try to conserve it.

92
00:05:25,581 --> 00:05:28,292
We're drinking your bending water?

93
00:05:28,417 --> 00:05:30,127
( SMACKS LIPS )

94
00:05:30,211 --> 00:05:32,338
You used this on the swamp guy!

95
00:05:32,421 --> 00:05:34,549
- Ugh!
- It does taste swampy.

96
00:05:34,841 --> 00:05:36,843
( SMACKING LIPS, BURPS )

97
00:05:36,968 --> 00:05:39,136
I'm sorry, it's all we have.

98
00:05:39,387 --> 00:05:41,013
Not anymore, look.

99
00:05:45,309 --> 00:05:48,229
Sokka, wait, you shouldn't
be eating strange plants.

100
00:05:48,437 --> 00:05:50,189
( GULPING ) Ahh...

101
00:05:50,815 --> 00:05:52,608
There's water trapped inside these.

102
00:05:52,692 --> 00:05:54,902
- I don't know.
- Suit yourself.

103
00:05:54,986 --> 00:05:56,779
It's very thirst-quenching, though.

104
00:06:02,827 --> 00:06:04,495
( VOICE ECHOING ) Drink cactus juice.

105
00:06:04,579 --> 00:06:05,830
It'll quench you.

106
00:06:06,038 --> 00:06:07,748
Nothing's quenchier.

107
00:06:07,832 --> 00:06:09,750
It's the quenchiest!

108
00:06:10,209 --> 00:06:12,295
Okay, I think you've had enough.

109
00:06:13,212 --> 00:06:15,006
Who lit Toph on fire?

110
00:06:15,464 --> 00:06:17,425
( PURRING )

111
00:06:17,508 --> 00:06:18,634
Unh!

112
00:06:18,801 --> 00:06:20,261
Can I get some of that cactus?

113
00:06:20,344 --> 00:06:21,971
I don't think that's a good idea.

114
00:06:22,054 --> 00:06:23,931
Come on, we need to find Aang.

115
00:06:27,226 --> 00:06:30,730
SOKKA: How did we get out here
in the middle of the ocean?

116
00:06:30,813 --> 00:06:31,814
KATARA: ( SIGHS )

117
00:06:41,365 --> 00:06:42,909
Appa!

118
00:06:48,039 --> 00:06:50,625
Appa!

119
00:06:56,964 --> 00:06:58,591
No...

120
00:07:00,551 --> 00:07:02,553
No!

121
00:07:10,645 --> 00:07:11,896
What is that?

122
00:07:11,979 --> 00:07:13,147
What, what is what?

123
00:07:13,230 --> 00:07:16,484
SOKKA: It's a giant mushroom.

124
00:07:16,734 --> 00:07:18,694
Maybe it's friendly!

125
00:07:19,111 --> 00:07:20,279
Let's just keep moving.

126
00:07:20,446 --> 00:07:21,656
I hope Aang's okay...

127
00:07:21,906 --> 00:07:23,616
( VOICE ECHOING ) Friendly mushroom!

128
00:07:23,699 --> 00:07:26,786
Mushy, giant friend!

129
00:07:29,747 --> 00:07:32,166
Yeah, a little, barefoot blind girl

130
00:07:32,249 --> 00:07:34,835
and her friends passed through here
a few days ago.

131
00:07:35,044 --> 00:07:37,964
Did they give you any indication
where they were headed?

132
00:07:38,965 --> 00:07:41,592
Maybe you could give me
a little incentive?

133
00:07:42,093 --> 00:07:45,262
You suggesting I break your fingers?

134
00:07:45,513 --> 00:07:47,056
They went in the desert.

135
00:07:47,139 --> 00:07:49,850
Too bad there's almost no chance
they survived.

136
00:07:50,184 --> 00:07:53,771
Mmm, that's okay,
'cause she's wanted dead or alive.

137
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,398
No, she's not.

138
00:07:55,481 --> 00:07:57,942
I'm certain her father wants her alive.

139
00:07:58,567 --> 00:07:59,610
Hey, look.

140
00:07:59,735 --> 00:08:02,405
Fire Nation wanted posters.

141
00:08:02,488 --> 00:08:03,531
So?

142
00:08:03,990 --> 00:08:06,951
So, look who's here.

143
00:08:25,886 --> 00:08:27,179
KATARA: I'm sorry, Aang.

144
00:08:27,304 --> 00:08:31,142
I know it's hard for you right now, but
we need to focus on getting out of here.

145
00:08:31,225 --> 00:08:32,309
What's the difference?

146
00:08:32,852 --> 00:08:34,353
We won't survive without Appa.

147
00:08:34,437 --> 00:08:35,604
We all know it.

148
00:08:35,855 --> 00:08:36,981
Come on, Aang.

149
00:08:37,064 --> 00:08:39,525
We can do this
if we work together, right, Toph?

150
00:08:39,859 --> 00:08:43,863
As far as I can feel, we're trapped
in a giant bowl of sand pudding.

151
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:45,406
I got nothin'.

152
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:48,367
Sokka, any ideas how to find Ba Sing Se?

153
00:08:48,492 --> 00:08:51,203
Why don't we ask the circle birds?

154
00:09:03,090 --> 00:09:05,968
-( PURRING )
-( LAUGHING SOFTLY )

155
00:09:08,012 --> 00:09:09,055
Ugh.

156
00:09:09,138 --> 00:09:12,266
We're getting out of this desert,
and we're gonna do it together.

157
00:09:12,349 --> 00:09:13,517
Aang, get up.

158
00:09:13,601 --> 00:09:14,685
Everybody, hold hands.

159
00:09:14,769 --> 00:09:17,772
We can do this. We have to.

160
00:09:19,065 --> 00:09:20,149
( LAUGHING )

161
00:09:20,232 --> 00:09:22,026
( PURRING )

162
00:09:25,905 --> 00:09:29,492
( WINGS BUZZING )

163
00:09:38,125 --> 00:09:39,919
I think we should stop for the night.

164
00:09:40,002 --> 00:09:42,129
ALL: ( GROANING )

165
00:09:43,172 --> 00:09:44,632
Is there any more water?

166
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:46,300
This is the last of it.

167
00:09:46,425 --> 00:09:48,511
Everyone can have a little drink.

168
00:09:50,846 --> 00:09:54,433
( SCREAMING ) Momo, no,
you've killed us all!

169
00:09:54,850 --> 00:09:56,727
KATARA: No, he hasn't.

170
00:09:56,894 --> 00:10:00,064
Oh, right, bending.

171
00:10:02,983 --> 00:10:05,569
Sokka, let me see the things
you got from the library.

172
00:10:05,653 --> 00:10:07,655
What? I didn't steal anything!

173
00:10:07,738 --> 00:10:08,989
Who told you that?

174
00:10:09,323 --> 00:10:10,366
It was you!

175
00:10:10,449 --> 00:10:13,244
You ratted me out!

176
00:10:14,245 --> 00:10:16,247
Sokka, I was there.

177
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,333
AANG: It doesn't matter.

178
00:10:20,042 --> 00:10:22,253
None of those will tell us where Appa is.

179
00:10:22,378 --> 00:10:25,714
No, but we can find out
which way Ba Sing Se is.

180
00:10:26,173 --> 00:10:28,217
We can use the stars to guide us.

181
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:31,846
That way, we can travel at night
when it's cool, and rest during the day.

182
00:10:32,221 --> 00:10:33,430
( SIGHS )

183
00:10:35,224 --> 00:10:36,851
Just try to get some sleep.

184
00:10:36,934 --> 00:10:39,562
We'll start again in a few hours.

185
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:44,150
No one here is gonna help us.

186
00:10:44,275 --> 00:10:46,402
These people just look like
filthy wanderers.

187
00:10:46,902 --> 00:10:48,154
So do we.

188
00:10:49,029 --> 00:10:52,199
Ah, this is interesting.

189
00:10:52,741 --> 00:10:56,078
I think I've found our friend.

190
00:10:57,788 --> 00:11:00,082
You brought us here to gamble on Pai Sho?

191
00:11:00,457 --> 00:11:03,544
I don't think this is a gamble.

192
00:11:05,462 --> 00:11:06,714
Let's take them now.

193
00:11:07,006 --> 00:11:09,592
This place is full of
desperate characters.

194
00:11:09,675 --> 00:11:12,469
If they find out
we're collecting a bounty,

195
00:11:12,553 --> 00:11:15,890
we might have to fight them all,
just to keep our prize.

196
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,725
Patience.

197
00:11:19,685 --> 00:11:21,395
May I have this game?

198
00:11:22,271 --> 00:11:24,982
The guest has the first move.

199
00:11:28,319 --> 00:11:31,322
I see you favor the White Lotus Gambit.

200
00:11:31,405 --> 00:11:33,824
Not many still cling to the ancient ways.

201
00:11:34,825 --> 00:11:38,120
Those who do can always find a friend.

202
00:11:38,412 --> 00:11:40,164
Then let us play.

203
00:11:56,222 --> 00:11:57,598
Welcome, brother.

204
00:11:57,765 --> 00:12:01,602
The White Lotus opens wide
to those who know her secrets.

205
00:12:02,144 --> 00:12:04,855
What are you old gasbags talking about?

206
00:12:04,939 --> 00:12:10,611
I always tried to tell you
that Pai Sho is more than just a game.

207
00:12:12,488 --> 00:12:16,075
I'm not waiting all night
for these geezers to finish yapping!

208
00:12:17,534 --> 00:12:19,286
It's over!

209
00:12:19,370 --> 00:12:21,538
You two fugitives are coming with me.

210
00:12:21,664 --> 00:12:23,207
I knew it!

211
00:12:23,582 --> 00:12:27,002
You two are wanted criminals
with a giant bounty on your heads!

212
00:12:27,211 --> 00:12:28,796
I thought you said he would help.

213
00:12:28,879 --> 00:12:31,173
He is, just watch.

214
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:34,426
You think you're going to capture them
and collect all that gold?

215
00:12:34,593 --> 00:12:35,886
Gold?

216
00:12:41,183 --> 00:12:43,143
Uh, maybe we shouldn't...

217
00:12:47,773 --> 00:12:49,233
( GRUNTING )

218
00:12:50,276 --> 00:12:51,568
( GRUNTS )

219
00:13:04,999 --> 00:13:06,000
( GRUNTS )

220
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:08,252
( SCREAMING )

221
00:13:12,631 --> 00:13:14,633
( MOANING )

222
00:13:14,717 --> 00:13:17,094
KATARA: Come on, get up, we need to go.

223
00:13:19,972 --> 00:13:21,015
( SMACKING LIPS )

224
00:13:21,515 --> 00:13:23,976
Yesterday, my mouth tasted like mud.

225
00:13:24,393 --> 00:13:26,061
Now, it just tastes like sand.

226
00:13:26,186 --> 00:13:29,356
I never thought
I'd miss the taste of mud so much.

227
00:13:30,024 --> 00:13:31,066
AANG: I'm awake.

228
00:13:31,191 --> 00:13:32,776
I couldn't sleep.

229
00:13:33,527 --> 00:13:36,947
Well, we need to get moving
if we want to get out of this sand pit.

230
00:13:38,824 --> 00:13:39,825
Appa!

231
00:13:39,908 --> 00:13:40,993
SOKKA: Appa?

232
00:13:41,076 --> 00:13:43,078
But why would Princess Yue need him?

233
00:13:43,162 --> 00:13:46,373
She's the moon, she flies by herself.

234
00:13:49,501 --> 00:13:51,128
It's just a cloud.

235
00:13:51,253 --> 00:13:53,130
Wait, a cloud!

236
00:13:53,213 --> 00:13:57,301
Here, fly up and bend the water
from that cloud into my pouch.

237
00:14:14,985 --> 00:14:16,945
Wow, there's hardly any in here.

238
00:14:17,029 --> 00:14:18,614
AANG: ( SHOUTING ) I'm sorry, okay?

239
00:14:18,697 --> 00:14:20,574
It's a desert cloud, I did all I could.

240
00:14:20,657 --> 00:14:21,867
What's anyone else doing?

241
00:14:21,950 --> 00:14:23,285
What are you doing?

242
00:14:24,912 --> 00:14:26,997
Trying to keep everyone together.

243
00:14:27,456 --> 00:14:28,832
Let's just get moving.

244
00:14:28,916 --> 00:14:30,417
We need to head this direction.

245
00:14:33,587 --> 00:14:35,130
Ow!

246
00:14:35,464 --> 00:14:39,218
Crud, I am so sick of
not feeling where I'm going.

247
00:14:39,802 --> 00:14:42,971
And what idiot buried a boat
in the middle of the desert?

248
00:14:43,055 --> 00:14:44,098
A boat?

249
00:14:44,181 --> 00:14:47,351
Believe me, I kicked it hard enough
to feel plenty of vibrations.

250
00:14:47,434 --> 00:14:48,519
( MOANS )

251
00:14:58,445 --> 00:15:01,115
KATARA: It's one of the gliders
the sandbenders use.

252
00:15:01,532 --> 00:15:03,951
And look, it's got
some kind of compass on it.

253
00:15:04,410 --> 00:15:06,453
I bet it can point us out of here.

254
00:15:07,996 --> 00:15:10,666
Aang, you can bend a breeze
so we can sail it.

255
00:15:10,749 --> 00:15:11,834
We're gonna make it!

256
00:15:12,876 --> 00:15:14,461
( LAUGHING )

257
00:15:14,545 --> 00:15:15,671
( PURRS )

258
00:15:24,430 --> 00:15:26,098
It is an honor to welcome

259
00:15:26,181 --> 00:15:29,184
such a high-ranking member
of the Order of the White Lotus.

260
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,729
Being a grand master,
you must know so many secrets.

261
00:15:33,772 --> 00:15:37,151
Now that you've played Pai Sho,
are you gonna do some flower arranging?

262
00:15:37,234 --> 00:15:39,862
Or is someone in this club
gonna offer some real help?

263
00:15:40,195 --> 00:15:42,281
You must forgive my nephew.

264
00:15:42,573 --> 00:15:48,245
He is not an initiate, and has
little appreciation for the cryptic arts.

265
00:15:51,165 --> 00:15:52,875
Who knocks at the guarded gate?

266
00:15:53,083 --> 00:15:56,753
One who has eaten the fruit
and tasted its mysteries.

267
00:16:03,927 --> 00:16:05,596
I'm afraid it's members only.

268
00:16:05,762 --> 00:16:07,306
Wait out here.

269
00:16:11,268 --> 00:16:12,936
( SNIFFS )

270
00:16:21,778 --> 00:16:25,115
KATARA: The needle on this compass
doesn't seem to be pointing north,

271
00:16:25,199 --> 00:16:26,617
according to my charts.

272
00:16:26,992 --> 00:16:28,911
( DREAMILY ) Take it easy, little lady.

273
00:16:28,994 --> 00:16:33,207
I'm sure the sand folks who built this
baby know how to get around here.

274
00:16:33,749 --> 00:16:34,958
( GASPS )

275
00:16:35,083 --> 00:16:37,377
KATARA: That's what the compass
is pointing to.

276
00:16:37,503 --> 00:16:38,670
That giant rock.

277
00:16:38,795 --> 00:16:40,964
It must be the magnetic center
of the desert.

278
00:16:41,048 --> 00:16:42,299
A rock?

279
00:16:42,424 --> 00:16:43,842
Yes, let's go!

280
00:16:43,967 --> 00:16:45,969
Maybe we can find some water there.

281
00:16:46,094 --> 00:16:48,263
Maybe we can find some sandbenders.

282
00:16:58,690 --> 00:17:01,235
Ah, finally.

283
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:04,530
Solid ground.

284
00:17:08,909 --> 00:17:10,953
SOKKA: ( BREATHING DEEPLY )

285
00:17:11,036 --> 00:17:13,914
I think my head is starting
to clear out the cactus juice.

286
00:17:14,998 --> 00:17:17,668
And look!

287
00:17:17,793 --> 00:17:20,337
( BOTH SPUTTERING )

288
00:17:20,462 --> 00:17:22,673
Tastes like rotten penguin meat.

289
00:17:23,173 --> 00:17:25,425
Oh, I feel woozy.

290
00:17:25,717 --> 00:17:28,053
You've been hallucinating
on cactus juice all day,

291
00:17:28,178 --> 00:17:32,099
and then you just lick something
you find stuck to the wall of a cave?

292
00:17:32,182 --> 00:17:33,892
I have a natural curiosity.

293
00:17:34,601 --> 00:17:36,478
I don't think this is a normal cave.

294
00:17:37,145 --> 00:17:38,981
This was carved by something.

295
00:17:39,273 --> 00:17:42,234
AANG: Yeah, look at the shape.

296
00:17:42,818 --> 00:17:45,028
TOPH: There's something buzzing in here.

297
00:17:45,237 --> 00:17:46,863
Something that's coming for us!

298
00:17:50,826 --> 00:17:51,868
( SCREAMING )

299
00:17:51,952 --> 00:17:53,203
( WINGS BUZZING )

300
00:18:02,504 --> 00:18:03,630
( INSECT SHRIEKING )

301
00:18:08,218 --> 00:18:09,469
( SCREECHES )

302
00:18:11,305 --> 00:18:12,681
TOPH: ( GRUNTS )

303
00:18:13,098 --> 00:18:14,266
Oh!

304
00:18:14,391 --> 00:18:15,517
What are you doing?

305
00:18:15,642 --> 00:18:17,144
That rock almost crushed me.

306
00:18:17,269 --> 00:18:19,771
Sorry, I can't tell
where they are in the air.

307
00:18:19,855 --> 00:18:20,981
I got this one.

308
00:18:21,231 --> 00:18:23,191
( SCREAMING )

309
00:18:23,275 --> 00:18:25,068
KATARA: Sokka, there's nothing there.

310
00:18:25,235 --> 00:18:26,403
Huh?

311
00:18:26,945 --> 00:18:29,114
I guess my head's not as clear
as I thought.

312
00:18:29,197 --> 00:18:30,866
KATARA: We have to get out of here.

313
00:18:30,949 --> 00:18:32,701
I'm completely out of water to bend.

314
00:18:32,784 --> 00:18:33,869
MOMO: ( SCREECHES )

315
00:18:33,952 --> 00:18:35,120
AANG: Momo!

316
00:18:35,621 --> 00:18:37,664
I'm not losing anyone else out here.

317
00:18:41,501 --> 00:18:43,170
Come on, we're going down.

318
00:18:44,504 --> 00:18:45,964
( INSECT SHRIEKS )

319
00:18:46,048 --> 00:18:47,966
KATARA: Toph, shoot a rock, right there.

320
00:18:48,050 --> 00:18:49,551
Fire!

321
00:18:50,052 --> 00:18:51,219
( SCREECHES )

322
00:18:51,345 --> 00:18:52,763
SOKKA: Yeah, you got it!

323
00:18:52,846 --> 00:18:53,930
She got it, right?

324
00:18:54,056 --> 00:18:56,183
Yes. Now, let's move.

325
00:18:59,144 --> 00:19:00,771
MOMO: ( CHATTERING )

326
00:19:06,443 --> 00:19:07,736
( GRUNTS )

327
00:19:09,488 --> 00:19:10,572
( CHATTERS )

328
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:20,374
( GRUNTING )

329
00:19:32,386 --> 00:19:33,804
KATARA: On your left.

330
00:19:34,054 --> 00:19:35,722
( INSECT SHRIEKS )

331
00:20:01,456 --> 00:20:03,500
What's going on? Is the club meeting over?

332
00:20:03,625 --> 00:20:05,919
Everything is taken care of.

333
00:20:06,461 --> 00:20:08,672
We're heading to Ba Sing Se.

334
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,298
Ba Sing Se?

335
00:20:10,424 --> 00:20:12,592
Why would we go to
the Earth Kingdom capital?

336
00:20:12,676 --> 00:20:14,594
The city is filled with refugees.

337
00:20:14,678 --> 00:20:16,346
No one will notice two more.

338
00:20:16,596 --> 00:20:18,932
We can hide in plain sight there.

339
00:20:19,182 --> 00:20:22,853
And it's the safest place
in the world from the Fire Nation.

340
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:25,856
Even I couldn't break through to the city.

341
00:20:25,939 --> 00:20:26,982
( DOOR OPENS )

342
00:20:27,065 --> 00:20:28,817
I have the passports for our guests,

343
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:31,570
but there are two men
out on the street looking for them.

344
00:20:34,406 --> 00:20:36,616
You seen these guys?

345
00:20:38,118 --> 00:20:41,621
MAN: What are you doing
in our land with a sandbender sailer?

346
00:20:41,705 --> 00:20:45,083
From the looks of it,
you stole it from the Hami tribe.

347
00:20:45,292 --> 00:20:47,461
We found the sailer
abandoned in the desert.

348
00:20:47,544 --> 00:20:49,421
We're traveling with the Avatar.

349
00:20:50,046 --> 00:20:53,467
Our bison was stolen,
and we have to get to Ba Sing Se.

350
00:20:53,592 --> 00:20:55,719
You dare accuse our people of theft,

351
00:20:55,802 --> 00:20:58,180
while you ride in on a stolen sand sailer?

352
00:20:58,263 --> 00:21:00,015
Quiet, Ghashiun!

353
00:21:00,098 --> 00:21:02,476
No one accused our people of anything.

354
00:21:02,559 --> 00:21:05,812
If what they say is true,
we must give them hospitality.

355
00:21:06,438 --> 00:21:07,647
GHASHIUN: Sorry, father.

356
00:21:07,981 --> 00:21:10,358
TOPH: I recognize the son's voice.

357
00:21:10,442 --> 00:21:12,861
He's the one that stole Appa.

358
00:21:13,236 --> 00:21:16,031
- Are you sure?
- TOPH: I never forget a voice.

359
00:21:16,490 --> 00:21:18,366
You stole Appa.

360
00:21:18,450 --> 00:21:20,368
Where is he? What did you do to him?

361
00:21:20,452 --> 00:21:22,788
They're lying. They're the thieves!

362
00:21:23,747 --> 00:21:25,040
( GRUNTING )

363
00:21:27,667 --> 00:21:30,003
Where is my bison?

364
00:21:38,887 --> 00:21:41,264
Hey, you. Where are these men?

365
00:21:41,389 --> 00:21:43,308
I got a tip that they're in your shop.

366
00:21:43,809 --> 00:21:46,853
As you can see, no one is here but us.

367
00:21:47,479 --> 00:21:50,232
We know all about your secret back room.

368
00:21:50,482 --> 00:21:52,526
Kick it down.

369
00:21:53,026 --> 00:21:54,903
Hey, that room is for flowers only.

370
00:21:59,866 --> 00:22:04,454
Some unlucky soul
has an incomplete Pai Sho set.

371
00:22:04,788 --> 00:22:09,376
( GRUNTING )
Let's go back to finding the girl.

372
00:22:18,927 --> 00:22:21,304
You tell me where he is, now!

373
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:25,100
What did you do?

374
00:22:25,183 --> 00:22:26,476
It wasn't me.

375
00:22:26,601 --> 00:22:28,854
TOPH: You said to put a muzzle on him.

376
00:22:28,937 --> 00:22:31,481
You muzzled Appa?

377
00:22:37,779 --> 00:22:38,822
GHASHIUN: I'm sorry!

378
00:22:38,947 --> 00:22:40,866
I didn't know it belonged to the Avatar!

379
00:22:40,949 --> 00:22:43,159
( IN DISTORTED VOICE )
Tell me where Appa is.

380
00:22:43,243 --> 00:22:45,203
I traded him to some merchants.

381
00:22:45,412 --> 00:22:47,998
He's probably in Ba Sing Se by now.

382
00:22:48,081 --> 00:22:49,958
They were gonna sell him there.

383
00:22:50,876 --> 00:22:53,003
Please, we'll escort you
out of the desert.

384
00:22:53,086 --> 00:22:54,546
We'll help however we can.

385
00:22:56,882 --> 00:22:59,801
SOKKA: Just get out of here, run!

386
00:23:47,807 --> 00:23:52,228
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
